  "failure_mode": {
    "title": "The model fills in details it cannot see",
    "summary": "Left alone, the 7B model made 3 field-level mistakes of one kind: it stated a detail the email does not contain. Given bare numbers such as '0.5 x 12 x 96' it answered units='in' and quoted the dimension string as evidence (2 RFQs). It also accepted 'same as PO 4471' as a certs value (1 RFQ). The checker rejects both patterns (a units value needs a quote containing a unit token; a reference to another order is not a value), lifting missing-spec recall from 23/26 to 26/26. At the RFQ level the naive rule was NOT confidently wrong on this set (0/30, same as the checker): all 3 of these RFQs also had a second, genuine gap that the model did flag, so they were blocked anyway. That is luck of the sample. Had units or the cert reference been the only gap, the RFQ would have gone to pricing (counterfactual, not observed here).",
    "examples": [
      {
        "id": "RFQ-004",
        "field": "units",
        "model_value": "in",
        "model_evidence": "0.5 x 12 x 96",
        "checker_reason": "units evidence quote contains no unit token",
        "truth": "missing",
        "other_gaps_still_flagged_by_naive": [
          "certs"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "RFQ-005",
        "field": "certs",
        "model_value": "same as PO 4471",
        "model_evidence": "Certs: same as PO 4471",
        "checker_reason": "value is a reference to another order, not a stated spec",
        "truth": "missing",
        "other_gaps_still_flagged_by_naive": [
          "finish"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "RFQ-008",
        "field": "units",
        "model_value": "in",
        "model_evidence": "1.25 OD x 1.5 long",
        "checker_reason": "units evidence quote contains no unit token",
        "truth": "missing",
        "other_gaps_still_flagged_by_naive": [
          "finish"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "residual_note": "The one remaining error is the reverse: on RFQ-014 the model returned no units even though the tolerance reads '+/- 0.001 in'. The checker flags units as missing, which costs one needless clarification question. That RFQ was already correctly blocked (dimensions are missing), and whether 'in' in a tolerance counts as stating units is itself a labelling-policy judgement call."
  },
